From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fil Dunsky <filipp.dunsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: compressed: use fatal FORTIFY field diagnostics

GCC 15 retains a run-time FORTIFY field-boundary check in the ATAG
command-line merge. The default warning uses WARN_ONCE, which requires
writable .data..once state and warn_slowpath_fmt. Neither is available
in the position-independent ARM decompressor, so the zImage link fails.

Use the existing fatal decompressor error path for these diagnostics.
Keep the FORTIFY checks enabled instead of discarding their state or
turning off hardening. Normal bounded copies retain their behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Fil Dunsky <filipp.dunsky@gmail.com>

---
AI assistance: Codex reproduced the GCC 15.3 object failure, implemented
this local compatibility fix and verified a Linux 6.18.64 zImage link.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/compressed/atags_to_fdt.c
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/compressed/atags_to_fdt.c
@@ -1,4 +1,10 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/* The decompressor has neither writable WARN_ONCE state nor printk. */
+#define fortify_warn_once(condition, ...) do { \
+	if (condition) \
+		error("detected field-spanning write"); \
+} while (0)
+
 #include <linux/libfdt_env.h>
 #include <asm/setup.h>
 #include <libfdt.h>
